;; The MELPA recipe for this package.
;;
;; MELPA's recipes live in its own repository, one file per package, named after
;; the package and with no extension. Submitting is a pull request there with a
;; copy of the form below; keeping the copy here means the submission is a copy
;; rather than a fresh guess about `:files', which is the field that gets it
;; wrong — the package is in a subdirectory of a monorepo, so the default
;; (top-level *.el) would find nothing at all.
;;
;; The list below is the same set `tools/emacs-package.mjs` puts in the release
;; tarball, and `emacs.test.mjs` fails if the two disagree. They did: this
;; recipe named three files where the package loads eight, so `ksav.el`'s own
;; `(require 'ksav-engine)` would have failed on the first load of a MELPA
;; install — in the one file whose comment is about `:files' being the field
;; that gets it wrong. The generator uses a denylist and maintains itself; a
;; hand-kept allowlist here is what drifted.
;;
;; `ksav-tests.el' is deliberately outside the glob. It is the package's real
;; suite and CI runs it against a live engine, but it wants `ert' and exists to
;; be run from a checkout; shipping it to every installation is a file nobody
;; loads. `ksav-services.el' and `ksav-release.el' are generated and must ship —
;; they are what the package requires of itself.

(ksav :fetcher github
      :repo "SYKhayyat/ksav"
      :files (
              "ksav/editors/emacs/ksav-services.el"
              "ksav/editors/emacs/ksav-release.el"
              "ksav/editors/emacs/ksav-engine.el"
              "ksav/editors/emacs/ksav-girsa.el"
              "ksav/editors/emacs/ksav-git.el"
              "ksav/editors/emacs/ksav-preview.el"
              "ksav/editors/emacs/ksav-write.el"
              "ksav/editors/emacs/ksav.el"
              "ksav/editors/emacs/README.md"))
